1. You would use the letter "A" in the English spelling of a whole number at 100,000,000 (one hundred million), where the word "hundred" contains an "A".

2. "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog." It is famous as a pangram, a sentence containing every letter of the English alphabet at least once.

3. Once upon a time, the three little pigs met the little red riding hood in the forest. They were building their homes and were surprised to see her. She told them about her journey, and they shared stories about their own adventures. Together, they laughed and enjoyed the day, learning that even different paths can lead to friendship. [end of text]


